  "player_text": "I leave the stranger their silence and look across the mud at the bright townhouse, checking its door, windows, and whether anyone there is watching the gate while the crowd pretends not to.",
  "visible_motivation": "They would not name anyone in the knot, only that someone keeps to themselves, and that house stands apart from the muddy crowd with colors the rain has not touched.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want to see if the house is closed up, occupied, or watching us, and whether it is the place people will not talk about.",
